# Build context for backend/Dockerfile is the PROJECT ROOT (needs both
# backend/ and frontend/ — see the Dockerfile's header comment for the
# exact build command). Docker only honors a .dockerignore at the context
# root, hence this file lives here rather than under backend/.
#
# IMPORTANT: unlike .gitignore, Docker's .dockerignore matcher does NOT
# treat a bare pattern (e.g. "*.env", "__pycache__/") as recursive — it only
# matches at the context ROOT. Verified with a minimal repro build during
# Phase 13: "*.env" let the real backend/.env (containing the actual
# JWT_SECRET and LLM_CLOUD_API_KEY) get COPY'd straight into the image, and
# "*.db" similarly let backend/data/app.db ship. Every pattern below that
# needs to match at any depth uses an explicit "**/" prefix.

# Virtual environment — rebuilt fresh inside the image from requirements.txt
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Git metadata — never needed inside the image
.git/
.gitignore

# Secrets — real .env files are never committed and must never be baked
# into an image either; config comes from env vars / --env-file at `docker run`
**/.env
**/*.env
!**/.env.example

# Databases — the container creates its own fresh SQLite DB on startup
# (init_db(), see app/db.py); a developer's local data.db must never ship.
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# MLOps local tracking store — large, and irrelevant to serving the app
**/mlruns/
**/mlartifacts/

# Python bytecode / caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# Test suite — never needed to SERVE the app; CI runs pytest separately
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml), never inside this image (Phase 13.1).
backend/tests/

# Editors / OS
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Raw training CSV — only backend/ml/train_model.py (a training-time
# script, never run inside the serving container) reads this; the already-
# trained model artifacts under backend/ml/model/ are copied in instead, so
# skipping the ~6MB CSV keeps the image leaner with no loss of function.
data/*.csv

# Claude Code / editor session state — never relevant to the image
.claude/
